  "id": "ah",
  "term": "AH",
  "definition": "AH stands for auditory hallucinations, meaning hearing sounds when there is no external sound present. In psychiatry and neurology, they are a clinically important and often distressing symptom seen not only in schizophrenia spectrum disorders but also in several other mental and neurological conditions.",
